
You should only need docker desktop installed, docker compose should download 
all the other stuff you need.

To start, run (first time might take a while):

  - docker compose up --build --detach

Once its finished, you access the site via http://localhost

You can test the backend with http://localhost/api/

And you can access the elasticsearch database with http://localhost/kibana
  - The username/password is "elastic" and "password"

To stop, run:
  - docker compose down 


It takes about a minute to start the full project with elastic search and kibana. 
If you don't want to do that, you can use the other compose.yaml files.

To run docker: 
- "docker compose -f ./compose.yaml --build --detach"
To stop: 
- "docker compose -f ./compose.yaml down"

Replace "compose.yaml" with whichever configuration you want.

compose.f.yaml runs only the frontend
compose.fb.yaml runs only the frontend and django backend
compose.fbe.yaml runs the frontend, backend, and elastic search, but not kibana


- "docker compose -f ./compose.f.yaml --build --watch" can be useful since it updates the frontend in real time

